+## Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile (`derived_pure_replay.v1`)
+
+State schema stays `2.1`; the profile is additive.
+
+- Selector
+  - `result_persistence_profile` is an optional top-level field of a root `state.json` and of each call-frame `state`. The only supported present value is `derived_pure_replay.v1`; any other value fails closed with a `ValueError` naming the profile, at `RunState` construction, at `StateManager.initialize(...)`, and on load (a failed load leaves the file byte-for-byte unchanged).
+  - Absent means the historical profile. `to_dict()` then omits the key, and loads never infer, backfill or upgrade the field.
+  - `StateManager.initialize(..., result_persistence_profile=None)` writes the field atomically with the new run state, before any visit. Generic callers stay explicit opt-in.
+  - Automatic selection: a successfully compiled typed `.orc` run (`orchestrator run`) and the new root created by `orchestrator resume --force-restart` select the profile; the force-restart source run is not modified. A fresh non-iterative child call frame selects it when the callee bundle's validated provenance has `frontend_kind == "workflow_lisp"` (never from the parent profile, a path suffix, an alias or a step identity). Existing roots and frames, non-Workflow-Lisp callees and iteration-owned child frames keep the historical profile. An existing frame whose `state` is missing or not a mapping is rejected with a `ValueError` mentioning `existing call-frame state` before anything is written.
+
+- Eligibility
+  - A node is replay-eligible when it is a compiler-generated `pure_projection`, acyclic, and visited at most once per scope. Recurrent, loop-owned and other multiply visited pure nodes keep full durable rows, bundles and checkpoints (`ineligible_pure_reasons[node] = multiple_visit_region`).
+  - The replay index (`orchestrator.workflow.pure_result_replay.derive_pure_result_replay_index`) is derived, never serialized, and never changes the runtime plan. Refs are scoped to the workflow that holds them; an imported callee bundle indexes only its own nodes under its own scope `root`.
+
+- Value-free completion shell
+  - A successful eligible pure step persists exactly `{"name", "step_id", "visit_count": 1, "status": "completed", "exit_code": 0, "outcome": {"status": "completed", "phase": "execution", "class": "completed", "retryable": false}, "result_storage": "derived_pure_replay.v1"}` and nothing else: no value, `artifacts`, `output`, `debug`, bundle or private lineage.
+  - Failed and skipped rows stay full durable rows.
+  - The visit and its running cursor are published by one atomic transaction (`begin_eligible_pure_visit`); settlement (`settle_eligible_pure_success` / `settle_eligible_pure_failure`) writes the row and clears the cursor in one transaction.
+  - Progress classification of a visit, cursor and row: `unstarted`, `interrupted`, `derived_complete`, `durable_failure_skip`, or `progress_witness_invalid` (any mismatch, including every visit other than 1).
+
+- Resume
+  - Before the prologue a resumed profiled scope audits its durable surfaces: a value row, pure bundle or private-lineage entry for an eligible node, or a checkpoint record or restore binding of an eligible node in the same scope, is a `profile_conflict`; invalid progress is `progress_witness_invalid`.
+  - Resume validates only the dependency leaves required by the restart boundary (bound inputs and durable intrinsics `exit_code`, `outcome.status|phase|class|retryable`), then re-derives needed pure values in memory over an overlay. Replay never dispatches an effect, increments a visit, settles a result or writes durable state. Failures are run errors of type `pure_result_replay_unavailable` with `context.reason` one of `durable_input_missing`, `durable_input_invalid`, `binding_unresolved`, `evaluation_failed`, `output_contract_invalid`, `progress_witness_invalid`, `dependency_index_invalid`, `reachability_ambiguous`.
+  - For a union pure result the transient row holds exactly the discriminant, the shared outputs and the active variant's outputs.
+  - The restart boundary is determined once per resume and passed to the default-resume decision.
+
+- Checkpoints
+  - Replay-eligible pure points emit no checkpoint record and are filtered from the candidates before unique-nearest selection; restore payloads omit derivable pure bindings. Filtering never skips past an invalid nearest durable boundary.
+  - Default resume admits one zero-record case: restore decision `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY` (mode `LEXICAL_CHECKPOINT_DEFAULT`, no checkpoint id, selection reason `validated_frame_entry_replay`), requiring validated bound-input leaves and exact profile and progress witnesses. Otherwise it fails closed with `lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`.
+
 ## Reusable-Call State Contract (v2.5)
 
 - Caller-visible exports
